  "title": "The Sound Between Us",
  "subtitle": "A Novel of Suspense",
  "authorDisplayName": "Liszt Think",
  "description": "Six months after her sister drowned near a remote hydrophone research station on the Norwegian coast, acoustic engineer Ingrid Solheim arrives to take her sister's old post. It is winter 1989. The sea ice is closing in. Five researchers winter at the outpost, and Ingrid knows one of them is lying. When she discovers the station's audio tapes have been altered—eleven minutes erased from the night of the drowning—Ingrid begins to listen. The clues are all around her: tide tables, a tape counter log, a diesel ledger, the small contradictions in her colleagues' accounts. Each has a motive. Each had the opportunity. As the Arctic darkness deepens and the station's isolation tightens, Ingrid must piece together what the sea refused to reveal. A psychological suspense novel of grief and detection, where every clue is on the page, and the killer is someone the reader has met.",
